ad0717e5f303717351b8851811e1d\nad390cfa0d65012ba451d1e66810fc90fe16b7c1\n3165ff19f98960cab0745ceaf78b9f303a57ea7e\n0faffa5ec1cb66a858d637e8215dbdfaa03c108f\n8434422e80eafe64b66a3594b50ff80b3f914dbb\n14d8e0cf21da8a88d45790791ad275a8192e36da\\nClone object baseline:\\ncount: 0\nsize: 0 bytes\nin-pack: 211662\npacks: 1\nsize-pack: 1.79 GiB\nprune-packable: 0\ngarbage: 0\nsize-garbage: 0 bytes\\nThe same SHA list and clean-rebuild/repack harness will be used for before/after measurement.","timestamp":1785693310178960001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Phase 4a test contract card:\\nauthoritative_contract: ticket A1 plus ADR 0026 (retain exact last-synced values; absent baseline degrades local-wins; corruption fails closed).\\ntrigger_preconditions: confirmed binding with five mirrored fields; repeat same baseline under two distinct clock values; contrast with a changed field and a present-null field; real second reconcile pass over unchanged fake Jira state.\\nproduction_path: BindingStore.set_baseline -> BindingStore.save; seed_baselines_from_snapshot; reconcile._advance_baselines -> commit helper in a real temp git tracker.\\ntest_tier: focused real-store unit for serialization/shape; existing stateful-fake integration strengthened for exact bindings bytes and HEAD commit identity. One tier lower cannot prove git commit suppression.\\nobservable_postcondition: no baseline_advanced_at, exact mirrored baseline including None, unchanged input preserves serialized bytes and tracker HEAD, changed input persists and changes bytes.\\nnegative_control: A->B baseline update must write.\\ncollateral_invariants: extraneous fields remain filtered, unbound is still no-op, version-1 and corrupt-store behavior unchanged.\\nci_gate: exact pytest nodes, then make test.\\nCurrent citations: BindingStore.set_baseline lines 451-464; _advance_baselines 520-536; inbound getattr call 257-260; seed caller 466-480. Prior line references are superseded.","timestamp":1785693326208336001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"A1 implementation evidence: standard-tier worker completed in 2 production-code attempts. Attempt 1 removed baseline_advanced_at; the orchestrator restored and ran the full oracle: 12/12 happy+edge+E2E checks passed. Exact-defect mutation (re-add the timestamp write) made all 4 held-out edge/E2E nodes RED; restoring it returned 4/4 GREEN. Review then caught the explicit compare-and-return guard missing, and attempt 2 added filtered-baseline equality early return while preserving present-null semantics; full oracle remained 12/12 GREEN. Process deviation: before the corrective dispatch, restored unit edge tests remained in the shared tree, and the worker ran the 11-test unit file despite being told not to inspect held-out material. The edge/E2E oracle had already independently passed against attempt 1, and the exact-defect mutation proof preceded this correction; record this transparently rather than claiming perfect hold-out isolation for attempt 2. Exact source-boundary search now finds no baseline_advanced_at in src/rebar. Module is 743 LOC under the hard 800 cap. Frozen 40-SHA packed-cost rebuild (clone tip d83e9277f420d0135c8e13e67101c53b671edc38, repack -Ad --window=250 --depth=50): before 13.84 KiB/version; A1 transform 2.33 KiB/version (16.8% of this baseline, below the <=25% / <=3.20 KiB gate). Scratch evidence: /private/tmp/rebar-a1-measure.H0rPNy.","timestamp":1785693885232969001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Final local verification before Gerrit: focused oracle 12 passed; exact-defect timestamp mutation forced the two fail-fast clock controls RED and restoration returned them GREEN; make lint PASS; make typecheck PASS; make test PASS (8519 passed, 39 skipped, 175 deselected, 17 warnings in 1873.03s). Independent five-axis review approved. First local rebar review-code PASS had one advisory that the equality guard is not behaviorally gated and timestamp controls looked inert. A private-identity assertion was deliberately rejected as a refactoring-litmus violation; timestamp controls were strengthened to fail-fast on any clock read, mutation re-proven, commit amended, and second review-code returned PASS with 0 blocking / 0 advisory. Commit 662e0f9 retains Change-Id Iaed6da2adffa9cb03e9cbc2f1e8ad739ad4e3e77, DCO, and resolved rebar-ticket trailer.","timestamp":1785696669274938001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Operator attestation for packed-cost AC (classification corrected after completion-verifier feedback). I ran the frozen 40-SHA corpus already recorded on this ticket from unfiltered clone tip d83e9277f420d0135c8e13e67101c53b671edc38. Before corpus: materialize each recorded bindings.json blob oldest-to-newest into a fresh git repo and commit all 40. After corpus: load the same blob at each SHA, remove baseline_advanced_at from every data['bindings'] entry, serialize with the production format json.dump(indent=2, sort_keys=True) plus newline, and commit in the same order into a second fresh repo. For each repo run git repack -Ad --window=250 --depth=50 after commit 1 and after commit 40, stat the single pack, and compute (pack_40-pack_1)/39/1024. Before: pack_1=3,115,474 bytes; pack_40=3,668,053; delta=552,579; marginal=13.84 KiB/version. After: pack_1=3,105,030; pack_40=3,197,938; delta=92,908; marginal=2.33 KiB/version. Ratio=16.8%, which passes the <=25% criterion (and is below 3.20 KiB against the ticket's fixed 12.79 KiB reference). All 40 transformed versions committed distinctly. Scratch repos remain at /private/tmp/rebar-a1-measure.H0rPNy; the durable evidence is this exact protocol, inputs, object sizes, formula, and result plus the prior ticket comment's ordered SHA list.","timestamp":1785699068165427001}],"created_at":1785372485409744001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"d3be2a7d-330c-48d4-84aa-ba51797c0574","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0247-619b-ea49-4ac8"},{"link_uuid":"b9ec37ac-23a8-45e5-b680-d8d760ec1345","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"0517-bb1d-0f56-4b77"},{"link_uuid":"0ba70af3-ae57-481b-9cf8-71cadf47e89d","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"7bc0-610a-dc7f-418a"}],"description":"## Outcome\nLanded as Gerrit change 1217 at merged commit `750a56b3b004f3c3f4cc1b456d3c56bd7809b87d`. `BindingStore.set_baseline` now filters the five mirrored fields, preserves keys whose value is `None`, returns early when the stored baseline is equal, and never reads the clock or writes `baseline_advanced_at`. This execution-state record supersedes planning-time line references while preserving the original rationale and acceptance contract.\n\n## Planning-time root cause and measured value\nBefore A1, `set_baseline` unconditionally replaced `entry[\"baseline\"]` and stamped `baseline_advanced_at = _now_iso()`. The stamp had no production reader. Across the original 40-revision study, baseline values changed 0 entries while the stamp changed 1,144 entries in a sort-ordered ~18 MB file, producing pathological git delta churn. The write-when-changed guard is byte-neutral for that historical corpus; the measured packed-cost win is from retiring the volatile stamp. Planning evidence lives in session log `1cb6-d553-6565-49b4`.\n\n## Implemented behavior and call sites\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py:451-466` owns filtering, equality comparison, early return, and changed-value assignment.\n- `BindingStore.seed_baselines_from_snapshot` begins at `binding_store.py:468` and delegates through the same guarded method.\n- `reconcile._advance_baselines` begins at `reconcile.py:520` and needs no caller edit because the guard is centralized.\n- The inbound-adopt dynamic call is at `apply_inbound_records.py:257-260` and receives the same centralized behavior.\n- Historical serialized stamp keys are inert; cleanup of cache history/current cache artifacts belongs to the parent epic rollout and rewrite, not to a new production reader or migration in A1.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] Two consecutive reconciler passes over unchanged Jira state preserve byte-identical `bindings.json`. Proved by `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py::test_unchanged_second_pass_preserves_binding_store_bytes_and_head`.\n- [x] The same integration test preserves the tracker HEAD, proving the unchanged second pass creates no commit. Run with `pytest tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py::test_unchanged_second_pass_preserves_binding_store_bytes_and_head`.\n- [x] Exact identifier search finds no production reference: `grep -Rnw baseline_advanced_at src/rebar` returns no match.\n- [x] Every new baseline written by `set_baseline` omits `baseline_advanced_at`; unit tests fail fast if baseline writes read the clock. Proved in `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_baseline.py`.\n- [x] A present-but-null baseline field round-trips as present. Proved by `test_present_null_baseline_field_round_trips`.\n- [x] A changed baseline persists the new value and changes serialized bytes, so the guard cannot degenerate into never-write. Proved by `test_changed_baseline_updates_serialized_bytes`.\n- [x] Repeated `seed_baselines_from_snapshot` input preserves serialized bytes, and the inbound-adopt path retains its existing focused coverage.\n- [x] The complete repository suite is green: `make test` passed with 8,519 passed, 39 skipped, and 175 deselected; `make lint` and `make typecheck` passed.\n- [x] [operator-attested] Marginal packed cost over the frozen 40-SHA corpus is at most 25% of baseline. Operator evidence on this ticket records the exact corpus, transformation, serializer, repack flags, pack byte counts, formula, and result: 13.84 KiB/version before versus 2.33 KiB/version after (16.8%).\n- [x] Gerrit change 1217 received `LLM-Review +1` and `Verified +1`, then merged without unresolved comments.\n\n## Files\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py` — implementation.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py` — read-only caller context.\n- `src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py` — read-only dynamic caller context.\n- `tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_baseline.py` — unit/serialization oracle.\n- `tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py` — stateful-fake git-backed E2E oracle.\n\nScope: completed A1 only; standalone follow-up story `deeb-89c1-1080-4690` owns plan-review evidence-kind classification.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/binding_store.py","reason":"implemented set_baseline equality guard and removed volatile stamp write"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/reconcile.py","reason":"read-only caller context for _advance_baselines"},{"path":"src/rebar/_engine/rebar_reconciler/apply_inbound_records.py","reason":"read-only inbound-adopt dynamic caller context"},{"path":"tests/unit/rebar_reconciler/state/test_binding_baseline.py","reason":"unit and real-serialization oracle for unchanged, changed, null, and seed behavior"},{"path":"tests/integration/rebar_reconciler/test_reconcile_idempotency.py","reason":"stateful-fake git-backed E2E oracle for bytes and commit identity"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"],["relates_to","0247-619b-ea49-4ac8"],["relates_to","0517-bb1d-0f56-4b77"],["relates_to","7bc0-610a-dc7f-418a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"a055f1e9-f9a2-49ca-9bb5-007543d6da81","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"f7ee-572b-1eb0-4af8","ticket_type":"story","title":"A1: delete the never-read baseline_advanced_at stamp and add a write-when-changed guard to set_baseline","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["8ed2bd93-3c82-4ea0-9a51-01c9286e0b27","e5a8813f-1794-4a2d-99c1-bdf5a243f07a","2996d347-ce55-4fc1-bd61-df54c74cf5a2","1994c9ea-9475-4202-96d9-b052a5137c13","082010c5-375f-4c77-a5f7-6f5260e7affe","5700e23b-88fa-4287-84ee-f9a39a0f9ae1","a055f1e9-f9a2-49ca-9bb5-007543d6da81","7bcba5f8-215f-4859-9faa-3212195e5c11","778b58b9-436b-4bfe-9e30-195807259a1f","e78b9e10-2853-4173-8f60-2b053d8dd8bc","f300c0e6-b364-4aba-9e46-71273942afaf","d3be2a7d-330c-48d4-84aa-ba51797c0574","b9ec37ac-23a8-45e5-b680-d8d760ec1345","5d04737f-28f3-4b10-804e-4dedae4d5de1","0ba70af3-ae57-481b-9cf8-71cadf47e89d","05e2e682-4d07-4168-a7bc-c33bae4cad89","9f74dbf8-4f5b-46ca-b058-537316a2fff4","ed9ae5d9-b3c6-4b73-8542-22dbb28b43ae","4662d15b-2705-463e-818b-cd7e93c24802","fdcae820-10bf-4a41-a865-f48b265c2ac2","6d31d5a2-4b85-4e60-879b-12bebe10274a"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785700821723425002,"uuid":"6e68826c-ca85-4e55-b989-5692c33ca65e"}